id: core/participation
title: "Participation in a Relationship"
kind: ontology-contract
record_shape: header
status: draft
version: 0.1.0
updated: 2026-09-30
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Codex, reconciling the relationship-core proposal on behalf of the maintainer"

purpose: >
  Separate who or what is addressable from how that referent is involved in a
  particular Relationship, Arena, or episode.

definition: >
  Participation is a time-indexed record of a referent's involvement in a
  Relationship. It records role, standpoint, presence, and applicable access
  or authority references without claiming more than the available evidence.

distinctions:
  referent: "Who or what can be addressed in the model."
  participation: "How that referent is involved here, during this episode."
  role: "The position a participation occupies; a role is not a new Agent or a grant of authority."
  standpoint: "The location from which a representation is produced; it is not a view from nowhere."
  presence: "Whether an actual participation is present, remote, or unknown. Historical, source-represented, and unavailable referents belong in attribution or absence records, not a live Participation."

rules:
  - "A participant roster MUST NOT substitute for an attributed relationship record."
  - "A quoted speaker, historical subject, source author, or modeled perspective is not a live participant unless a separate participation record establishes present involvement."
  - "A role does not create identity, consent, authority, or independent corroboration."
  - "A participation can end, pause, or change without changing the relationship identity."
  - "Private standpoint material remains governed by current disclosure boundaries, including during replay."

links:
  - schemas/participation.v0.1.schema.json
  - schemas/relationship.v0.1.schema.json
  - core/relationship.yawn
  - spec/ontology.md

proof:
  covers: [definition, distinctions, rules]
  tests:
    - tests/relationship-core-v0.1.test.mjs
  status: proposed-until-maintainer-review
